BT /F2 9.0 Tf 65.00 758.00 Td (* Challenge 1: Ollama phi3.5 CPU Throughput & Labeling 3,000 Commands) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 745.00 Td (Problem: Running phi3.5-mini-instruct locally on a single CPU thread to label 3,000 commands) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 733.00 Td (projected an execution time of over 6.5 hours, threatening project deadlines.) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 718.00 Td (Solution: I engineered a stateless worker sharding architecture in worker/worker.py. By) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 706.00 Td (spawning multiple parallel worker pods in the 'pipeline' namespace using a deterministic modulo) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 694.00 Td (strategy \(line_index % SHARD_COUNT == SHARD_INDEX\), the workload was partitioned seamlessly) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 682.00 Td (with zero overlapping records and zero gaps.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.0 Tf 65.00 667.00 Td (* Challenge 2: PyTorch Container Image Size Constraints \(< 2 GB\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 654.00 Td (Problem: Standard PyTorch wheels bundle extensive CUDA runtime libraries, producing Docker) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 642.00 Td (images in excess of 6.2 GB, far exceeding the strict 2.0 GB submission limit.) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 627.00 Td (Solution: I leveraged PyTorch's specialized CPU-only wheel repository \(--extra-index-url) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 615.00 Td (https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu\) inside a multi-stage python:3.10-slim Dockerfile. This) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 603.00 Td (reduced the final image size to 842 MB \(a 86% reduction\) while satisfying all runtime) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 591.00 Td (dependencies.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9.0 Tf 65.00 576.00 Td (* Challenge 3: Stateless NACL Asymmetric Return Traffic Blockage) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 563.00 Td (Problem: In Task 5, initial packet simulations dropped outbound client replies despite valid) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 551.00 Td (inbound HTTP rules.) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 536.00 Td (Solution: Unlike stateful security groups, stateless NACLs require explicit return rules. I) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 524.00 Td (added outbound rules for ephemeral port ranges \(1024-65535\) and placed the malicious subnet) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.0 Tf 75.00 512.00 Td (deny rule \(198.51.100.0/24\) at rule number 100, ensuring malicious traffic is dropped before) Tj ET
